@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch09ch10-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch09ch10-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 9 and 10"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.4.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch09ch10-lineage/1.4.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch09ch10_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.4.0 (2026-11-08): Backlog stage. Carries forward ST_CI5_Research_Ch09, TK_Ret_Ch09_Research, TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Verify from the closed Lineage2 (closure report CLOSURE_REPORT_sen0414_slides_lineage_Lineage2_v1_0_0.md); adds the chapter-check, draft, owner-approval-gate and (blocked) render tasks for chapters 9 and 10; adds a Proposed item asking whether the YA-suffixed legacy decks for these two chapters' subjects (regex, reading/writing files) can be retired."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "1.3.0 (2026-11-08): Objective stage - two objectives (owner-approved drafts: 0 to 2; chapter checks read and recorded: 0 to 2), each with its metric, baseline and target."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "1.2.0 (2026-11-08): Goal stage - two goals, one per scope deliverable (the draft, the checked-and-fixed materials), each facing the mission."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "1.1.0 (2026-11-08): Scope stage - areas, deliverables and exclusions stated taxonomically per G194; chapters 1-8 and all chapters other than 9-10 excluded by name."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "1.0.0 (2026-11-08): Mission stage - mission settled per the handover's suggested wording, scoped to the smallest closeable slice (chapters 9-10 only), course-wide mission kept separate in the closed Lineage2's closure report."@en .

## --- Profile declaration (ceremony step 1) ---

ex:ProfileDecl a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work and this lineage names none other. Level L2 (not L4) is declared because this lineage does not yet re-run the full SHACL/register tooling used by the BRSF framework's own self-governance (oe_release, backlog_lineage_*_check) against this course repository's simplified lineage files - a narrower claim stated plainly, not a higher one assumed." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-12"^^xsd:date .

## --- Lineage ---

ex:Lineage3 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 9 and 10, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission3 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 3 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_InProgress ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 is the closed SEN0414 slides lineage (07-lineage/sen0414_slides_lineage_v2_402_0.ttl); this lineage carries forward only the chapter-9/10 slice of its open scope, per CLOSURE_REPORT_sen0414_slides_lineage_Lineage2_v1_0_0.md."@en .

## --- Mission ---

ex:Mission3 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 9 and 10 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog3 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 9 and 10 of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft, ready for the lecture of the week of 2026-11-12." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Suggested by the handover HANDOVER_session_to_next-session_chapters-9-10-fresh-lineage_v1_0_0.md (2026-11-08), settled as the mission statement in this stage, following the owner's standing preference for lineages scoped to the smallest closeable slice rather than the whole package." .

## --- Scope (taxonomic: areas, deliverables, exclusions - G194) ---

ex:Scope3 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Draft, check and (on approval) render chapters 9-10 only"@en ;
    backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission3 ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area3_StateCheck, ex:Area3_Draft, ex:Area3_Render ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl3_Ch1to8, ex:Excl3_OtherChapters, ex:Excl3_ExamWork, ex:Excl3_RenderBeforeApproval ;
    backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del3_ApprovedDraft, ex:Del3_CheckedMaterials ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: for chapters 9 (Regular Expressions) and 10 (Reading and Writing Files) of the 3rd edition only - (a) read the existing deck, page, research/ABox and chapter-check state and say plainly what is stale, missing, or duplicated; (b) write one plain-text chapter draft per chapter (story per 5N1K, explanations, slide outline, page-tab outline in slide order, each code example with its executed result, resources slide) for the owner's reading and approval; (c) ONLY after approval, render the deck, page and document from that one draft, versioned per the 2026-11-08 version rule (each file its own step, sized to the change). OUT: chapters 1-8 (midterm scope, not touched this week); chapters 11 and onward (later narrow lineages); exam and mock-exam work (held outside this repository); rendering before the owner's approval of the draft." .

ex:Area3_StateCheck a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "What exists for chapters 9-10 today"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 .
ex:Area3_Draft a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "The one approved draft per chapter"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 .
ex:Area3_Render a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Deck, page and document rendered from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 .

ex:Del3_ApprovedDraft a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Owner-approved plain-text draft, chapters 9 and 10"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Draft .
ex:Del3_CheckedMaterials a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapter-9/10 materials checked against current standard, gaps named"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_StateCheck .

ex:Excl3_Ch1to8 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 1-8 (midterm scope)"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Owner's explicit order 2026-11-08: do not touch Chapters 1-8 this week." .
ex:Excl3_OtherChapters a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 11-25 and the chapter-1-8/chapter-9-research retrofit"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages (handover S2); the earlier-chapter retrofit is a later one." .
ex:Excl3_ExamWork a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exam and mock-exam work"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Held outside this repository; midterm already held in full attendance." .
ex:Excl3_RenderBeforeApproval a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Rendering a deck/page/document before the draft is approved"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The draft-first rule (owner-agreed, handover S4): layout built before content is settled is the measured cause of the five-build-per-page slowness; rendering is blocked on approval." .

## --- Goals ---

ex:G3_DraftApproved a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "Each chapter has one owner-approved draft"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:Area3_Draft ;
    backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission3 ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Direct reading of the mission statement and of the handover's draft-first order (S4): the draft, approved, is what the mission requires before rendering." .

ex:G3_StateChecked a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "What exists for chapters 9-10 is read and its gaps named before building"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:Area3_StateCheck ;
    backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission3 ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Handover S3: 'the work is to check what exists against the owner's current teaching emphasis and standards and fix the gaps, not to start from nothing. Say plainly what you find stale or missing before you build.'" .

## --- Objectives ---

ex:Obj3_DraftsApproved a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Owner-approved drafts: from 0 to 2"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3_DraftApproved ; backlog:fillsScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasSuccessMetric ex:Met3_DraftsApproved ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count of chapter-9/10 plain-text drafts the owner has approved, read from his reply in this conversation." ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasForecastDate "2026-11-10"^^xsd:date ; backlog:hasForecastRationale "Handover S4: 'draft for the owner's reading by 2026-11-10, so that rendering and checking have two days.' A forecast at the pace delivered, not a target, deadline or promise (lineage discipline step 3)." ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
ex:Met3_DraftsApproved a backlog:Metric ; rdfs:label "owner-approved chapter-9/10 drafts"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 .
ex:Obs0_Obj3_DraftsApproved a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Baseline, before any draft is read"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met3_DraftsApproved ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj3_DraftsApproved ; backlog:hasObservedValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony true ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "No draft has been sent to the owner yet; this version carries the two drafts for his reading, not yet his approval." .

ex:Obj3_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Chapter checks read and recorded: from 0 to 2"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3_StateChecked ; backlog:fillsScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasSuccessMetric ex:Met3_StateChecksRecorded ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count of chapters (of 9, 10) whose existing deck/page/research state has been read against the current standard and its gaps named in writing." ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
ex:Met3_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:Metric ; rdfs:label "chapter-9/10 state checks recorded"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 .
ex:Obs1_Obj3_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Measured this turn: both chapters read"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met3_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj3_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:hasObservedValue "2"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony false ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Read 07-lineage/sen0414_slides_lineage_v2_401_0.ttl for the real hasState history of every chapter-9/10-named item (not the first occurrence - the last, since corrections are appended, never edited); inspected both .pptx decks (slide/chart/media counts) and the newest page of each chapter; findings recorded on ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch09 and ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch10 below, at target already." .

## --- Backlog ---

ex:Backlog3 a backlog:Backlog ; rdfs:label "Work admitted for chapters 9-10"@en ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "Backlog_SEN0414_Ch09Ch10" ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:isRegisterRoot true ;
    backlog:hasMember ex:ST3_StateCheck, ex:ST3_DraftCh09, ex:ST3_DraftCh10, ex:ST3_ApprovalGate, ex:ST3_RenderCh09, ex:ST3_RenderCh10, ex:ST3_YaRetirement,
        ex:ST_CI5_Research_Ch09_Carried .

## Carried forward from the closed Lineage2 (unchanged identifiers, re-parented)
ex:ST_CI5_Research_Ch09_Carried a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Research set and first page ABox of chapter 9 (carried forward)"@en ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_CI5_Research_Ch09" ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:carriedForwardFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Carried, ex:TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Verify_Carried ;
    backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:hasState backlog:Ready ;
    rdfs:comment "Same work item as ex:ST_CI5_Research_Ch09 in Lineage2 (last state Ready, per the last hasState assertion in the file, not the first); re-parented here per the closure report's disposition table. Not started this turn - the chapter check (ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch09) read the deck and page directly; this research/ABox retrofit pass is separate backend work, named so it is not lost." .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Carried a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make the research set and first page ABox of chapter 9 pass the chapter check (carried forward)"@en ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ret_Ch09_Research" ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:carriedForwardFrom ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Ready .
ex:TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Verify_Carried a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Verify the research set and page ABox of chapter 9 (carried forward)"@en ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Verify" ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:carriedForwardFrom ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Ready ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Ret_Ch09_Research_Carried .

## New work, this lineage
ex:ST3_StateCheck a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Read what exists for chapters 9-10 and name the gaps"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_StateCheck" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del3_CheckedMaterials ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch09, ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch10 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done .
ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch09 a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Chapter 9 state check"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK3_StateCheck_Ch09" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck SEN0414_Ch09_RegularExpressions_3e_v2_0_0.pptx: 48 slides, 7 native charts, 4 media (story images). Page sen0414_ch09_page_v9_90_0.html exists (five builds to 9.90.0) with the current standard's sections present (Stories from the record, Resources, Chapter code, Mock exam, Quiz, etc.). Gap found: the research/ABox retrofit against the current chapter-check standard that chapters 10-18 went through in Iteration 20 was planned for chapter 9 (ex:ST_CI5_Research_Ch09 and its two tasks) but never started - last recorded state Ready, not Done. A legacy duplicate exists: 03-materials/slides/Chapter7PatternMatchingWithRegularExpressions_YA_v1_0_0.pptx (old-edition numbering, same subject, superseded by the current ch09 deck) - candidate for retirement, see ex:ST3_YaRetirement." .
ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch10 a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Chapter 10 state check"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK3_StateCheck_Ch10" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck SEN0414_Ch10_ReadingWritingFiles_3e_v2_0_0.pptx and page sen0414_ch10_page_v9_95_0.html were fully taken through the Iteration-20 retrofit pipeline and controlled (evidence ex:Ev2_Ctl_deck10, ex:Ev2_Ctl_page10, ex:Ev2_Ctl_research10 in the closed Lineage2's register: deck standard check PASS=13/FAIL=0, overlap check CLEAN, 18/18 examples reproduce their recorded result, page test 9.37.0 402 features passed/0 failed, chapter check Research/Ch10 PASS). No open gap against the current standard found. A legacy duplicate exists: 03-materials/slides/Chapter8ReadingAndWritingFiles_YA_v1_0_0.pptx (old-edition numbering, same subject) - candidate for retirement, see ex:ST3_YaRetirement." .

ex:ST3_DraftCh09 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Plain-text chapter draft, chapter 9"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_DraftCh09" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_DraftsApproved ; backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del3_ApprovedDraft ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch09 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Draft written this turn for the owner's reading; not yet owner-approved (that is ex:ST3_ApprovalGate)." .
ex:ST3_DraftCh10 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Plain-text chapter draft, chapter 10"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_DraftCh10" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_DraftsApproved ; backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del3_ApprovedDraft ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK3_StateCheck_Ch10 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Draft written this turn for the owner's reading; not yet owner-approved (that is ex:ST3_ApprovalGate)." .

ex:ST3_ApprovalGate a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Owner reads and approves (or corrects) both drafts"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_ApprovalGate" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_DraftsApproved ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:ST3_DraftCh09, ex:ST3_DraftCh10 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Ready ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Blocks ex:ST3_RenderCh09 and ex:ST3_RenderCh10 by the draft-first rule (ex:Excl3_RenderBeforeApproval). A correction after approval goes to the draft and is re-rendered, never patched in one output (handover S4.3)." .

ex:ST3_RenderCh09 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Render deck, page and document of chapter 9 from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_RenderCh09" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:dependsOn ex:ST3_ApprovalGate ; backlog:hasState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Each of the deck, page and document continues from its own last version (2026-11-08 version rule); run 08-tooling/cme_version_check_v1_0_0.py before release, declaring the size of each change." .
ex:ST3_RenderCh10 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Render deck, page and document of chapter 10 from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_RenderCh10" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:dependsOn ex:ST3_ApprovalGate ; backlog:hasState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Same version rule as chapter 9; chapter 10's deck/page are already at the Iteration-20 standard, so this is likely a smaller (patch/minor) step than chapter 9's." .

ex:ST3_YaRetirement a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Retire the YA-suffixed legacy decks for regex and reading/writing-files?"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST3_YaRetirement" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "03-materials/slides/Chapter7PatternMatchingWithRegularExpressions_YA_v1_0_0.pptx and Chapter8ReadingAndWritingFiles_YA_v1_0_0.pptx duplicate the subjects of the current ch09 and ch10 decks under the old edition's numbering. Not decided here - the handover asks only to 'say whether it can be retired', and retirement is irreversible-ish (file removal), so it is an owner question, not an agent decision (B2: act when a rule or the evidence already decides; ask when it is genuinely undecidable - there is no rule yet for retiring superseded legacy files)." .
